# Auto-Routing (No Orchestrator Wait)

Cursor runs as a single agent. Do not propose-and-wait. **Infer → load skill → execute.**

## Behavior

1. Parse user intent from natural language
2. Select lightest safe workflow (`zoo-routing.mdc`)
3. Load matching skill(s) and adopt role automatically
4. Execute in the same turn when safe
5. Auto-continue chains (implement → verify → review) unless blocked

## Ask only when

- Intent is genuinely ambiguous (offer numbered plain-language choices via `AskQuestion`)
- Irreversible action pending (commit, push, publish issues)
- Plan gate requires approval (non-tweak implementation)
- Workflow phase gate (feature PRD, fix hypothesis confirmation)

## Never

- Tell user to type `/zoo-*`
- Stop after proposing a workflow when intent is clear
- Use slash commands in selectable options

## Multi-phase handoffs

Switch role automatically between phases (architect → tweaker → architect). Persist state in `.scratch/{workflow}-state.json`.
